# Frozen 2026-09-15, the first run with `--ratchets` on: functions whose LAST
# statement is a conditional, reviewed and KEPT because the caller reads that
# status as an ANSWER, never as success. Two-way: a frozen function that stops
# ending on a conditional is STALE and its line goes.
# Format: <file>	<function>.
#
# maybe_truthy is a pure predicate - `is_truthy "${v,,}" || [[ "${v,,}" == y ]]`
# - and every call site is a condition (`if maybe_truthy "$RUN_CODEQL"`, in the
# three ci-container-run-*.sh drivers). A false answer is the point; returning 1
# is the contract, and making it `return 0` would turn every "false" flag into a
# "true" one.

scripts/linux/lib/container-steps.sh	maybe_truthy
